            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "Could not go BECAUSE the weather was stormy. BECAUSE introduces the reason. The reason comes AFTER 'because'.",
            "hints": [
              "The second half gives the REASON why the beach was impossible: the weather was too STORMY. Ask: which joining word introduces a reason? 'So' gives a result, and 'although' would signal a contrast instead."
            ]
