                "hint": "'SIX O'CLOCK' is an exact point on the clock. Ask: which preposition goes in front of clock times? Say each choice aloud before 'six o'clock' - only one sounds right.",
                "explanation": "Use AT for specific clock times: AT six o'clock, AT noon, AT midnight."
