                "hint": "The tunnel was driven through while the JOURNEY was still going on - the blank covers a whole stretch of time. Ask: which preposition means 'all through a period of time'?",
                "explanation": "DURING = throughout a period: DURING the journey, DURING the holiday, DURING the match."
