                "hint": "The blank sits right in front of the noun HUSBAND, so it must show who the husband belongs to - the uncle's wife. Ask: does a subject pronoun ever describe a noun? Only a possessive form can go before a noun.",
                "explanation": "Before 'husband' (a noun), use a POSSESSIVE ADJECTIVE: HER husband. 'She husband' is wrong."
