                "hint": "WHILE signals a longer action already running when she HEARD the moving stories, and the subject counts as ONE person. Ask: which past form shows an action still going on - a finished simple past, or a helper plus the -ing form?",
                "explanation": "'While she ___' = ongoing background past action = past continuous. She WAS HELPING when she heard the stories."
