                "hint": "The subject SEVERAL OF HER FRIENDS names more than one person, and they all did it in that same past week. Ask: which helper does a plural subject need in the past continuous - the singular one, or the plural one?",
                "explanation": "Several friends = plural. They were reading at the same time = WERE READING (past continuous)."
