            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": "NOBODY / EVERYONE / SOMEONE = Singular! Nobody OWNS = add -S. 'Nobody own' is WRONG. Singular indefinite pronouns always take singular present-tense verbs.",
            "hints": [
              "The subject is NOBODY, not 'our neighbourhood'. Words like nobody and everyone behave like ONE person. Ask: in the present tense, does a singular subject take the plain verb, or the one ending in -s?"
            ]
