            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "HAS + past participle = present perfect. The shelter HAS REHOMED two hundred dogs = started last year and still going. REHOME → REHOMED (regular verb, add -d).",
            "hints": [
              "HAS stands in front of the blank, and the time stretches SINCE IT OPENED LAST YEAR right up to today. Ask: after 'has', which form builds a present perfect - the plain verb, the -s form, the -ing form, or the past participle?"
            ]
