            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "The doorbell RANG = sudden past event. The dog was already in the middle of sleeping = WAS SLEEPING (past continuous). Was/were + verb-ing = action in progress when interrupted.",
            "hints": [
              "The DOORBELL RANG and STARTLED IT AWAKE - a sudden event breaking into something already happening. Ask: which choice shows an action still in progress in the past? A plain past verb only reports a finished action."
            ]
