            "id": "S22_G",
            "passage": "Twelve-year-old Jamal practised the same piano piece for four months. It was a difficult piece, full of fast runs and sudden changes in volume, and he knew every note by heart. Tonight was the school concert, and he was the closing act.\n\nWhen Jamal walked onto the stage, the lights were bright and the hall was packed. He sat at the grand piano, placed his hands on the keys and began.\n\nThe first half went perfectly. Then, in the third movement, his fingers slipped. He hit a wrong note — loud and clear in the quiet hall. He felt his face go red.\n\nBut Jamal did not stop. He steadied himself, took a breath and kept playing. The mistake faded behind him as the music carried on.\n\nWhen the last note rang out, there was a moment of silence. Then the audience erupted. They rose to their feet and clapped. His music teacher, Mr Chua, was standing at the side of the stage with a wide smile.\n\n'That was the bravest thing I have seen on this stage in twenty years,' Mr Chua said afterwards. 'Anyone can play a perfect piece. But only a true musician carries on after making a mistake.'",
