            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "HAS + past participle = present perfect. Our school HAS INTRODUCED fruit breaks = started in the past, still happening now. INTRODUCE → INTRODUCED (add -d for regular verbs ending in -e).",
            "hints": [
              "HAS, plus SINCE the beginning of last term: an action that started in the past and still runs today. Ask: after 'has', which form of the verb do we need - the plain verb, the -ing form, or the past participle?"
            ]
