            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "PLENTY OF = a large amount (works with both countable and uncountable nouns). 'Water' is uncountable → drink PLENTY OF water. MANY and A FEW are only for countable nouns.",
            "hints": [
              "WATER cannot be counted: you never say 'one water, two waters'. Ask: which quantity phrase works with an uncountable noun? 'Many', 'several' and 'a few' all count separate items one by one."
            ]
