            "passage": "Museums keep history alive. Every object on display is an (1)________ - something made or used by people in the past. Many items have been carefully (2)________ so that they do not decay: experts control the temperature and the light in every room. Some objects are only copies - a (3)________ made to look exactly like the original. Others are given by families who no longer wish to keep them, and each (4)________ is a generous gift to the public. Some exhibits date back to the fifth (5)________, over fifteen hundred years ago.",
