            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "The bridge BEGAN TO SWAY = sudden past event. Explorers were already in the middle of crossing = WERE CROSSING (past continuous). Was/were + verb-ing = action in progress when something interrupts.",
            "hints": [
              "The bridge BEGAN TO SWAY suddenly, cutting across something already happening. Ask: which choice shows an action in progress in the past? A plain past verb reports only a finished act, and a present form cannot fit."
            ]
