            "hint": "The given sentence is passive: THE SCHOOL'S NEW WEBSITE receives the action, and A TEAM OF STUDENT VOLUNTEERS does it. Ask: when the doer moves to the front, what happens to 'was' and to the word 'by'? The verb becomes a plain past form.",
            "explanation": "Active voice: AGENT + VERB + OBJECT. A team of student volunteers DESIGNED the school's new website. Remove 'was' and 'by' when converting passive to active.",
