            "passage": "Magic tricks work by fooling the mind rather than actually doing the impossible. The most important tool in a magician's craft is (1)________ of hand — the ability to move objects with the fingers so quickly and smoothly that the eye cannot follow. A magician also uses (2)________ to guide the audience's attention away from what is really happening. For example, a dramatic gesture with one hand draws the eyes while the other hand secretly performs the real action. The result is an (3)________ — a false image that the brain accepts as real because it sees what it expects to see. A skilled magician makes every (4)________ in the audience feel as though the impossible has just happened right in front of them. At the end of some shows, the magician may choose to (5)________ how a trick works, which often surprises audiences — because the method is usually much simpler than they imagined.",
