            "passage": "The school hall was full. Three hundred students sat in rows, facing a small stage lit by a single spotlight. On the stage stood a man in a black suit. He introduced himself as Marco.\n\nMarco performed seven tricks that evening. He made a coin pass through a solid table. He caused a handkerchief to change colour three times in a row. He invited a girl named Priya to choose any card from a deck, memorise it and return it to the pack — then he produced it from inside a sealed envelope that sat on a chair since the show began.\n\nBut the final trick was the one everyone remembered.\n\nMarco asked the audience to think of any number between one and ten. He did not ask anyone to say it out loud. Then he turned his back to the audience and said, 'The number most of you are thinking of is seven.'\n\nA roar went up from the hall.\n\nLater, a boy named Ethan asked his teacher how the trick worked. 'When people are asked for a number between one and ten,' his teacher said, 'most people choose seven. It's simply how the human brain tends to work.'\n\nEthan was quiet for a moment. 'So it wasn't really magic at all,' he said.\n\n'Perhaps not,' said the teacher. 'But it felt like it, didn't it?'",
