            "sentence": "Our school has ________ the inter-class relay trophy three years in a row.",
            "options": [
              "win",
              "wins",
              "won",
              "winning"
            ],
            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "HAS + past participle = present perfect. Our school HAS WON the trophy = it won it at some point and the result stands today.",
            "hints": [
              "HAS is already sitting in the sentence, waiting for its partner, and THREE YEARS IN A ROW reaches right up to today. Ask: after 'has', which form follows - plain, -s, -ing, or a past participle?"
            ]
