            "passage": "A river is a complex (1)________ — a community of living things that depend on each other and on the water around them for survival. The fish, insects, plants and mammals that live in a river all rely on the same clean water and food sources. The speed of the water, or (2)________, determines what kinds of animals can survive in different parts of the river. Slow-moving water supports different life forms from fast-flowing rapids. Many (3)________ animals — those that live in water — have developed special features such as gills, webbed feet or streamlined bodies to help them move and breathe underwater. Plants and certain organisms also (4)________ the river water naturally, removing dirt and impurities as the water passes through their roots and stems. When humans pollute a river, they destroy the natural (5)________ that many species depend on, threatening the survival of entire communities of wildlife.",
