            "answer": 2,
            "explanation": "SO MUCH + uncountable noun. 'Food' is uncountable → SO MUCH food. 'Many food' or 'a few food' are WRONG. Use MUCH/SO MUCH for uncountable things.",
            "hints": [
              "FOOD cannot be counted - there is no plural - and the result clause (THAT WE COULD NOT TRY EVERYTHING) tells you the amount was huge. Ask: which choice suits an uncountable noun inside that frame? 'A few' and 'several' need countable things."
            ]
