                "hint": "THE CHOICE IS YOURS: waiting is one path, taking a TAXI is the other, but you cannot do both. Ask: which box word offers two alternatives, only one of which will actually happen?",
                "explanation": "OR = a choice between two options. Wait for the rain OR take a taxi = choose one. AND would mean doing both. OR = alternative choice."
