              {
                "num": 7,
                "answer": "since",
                "hint": "Look at what follows the blank: THE FIRST RUMBLE AT NOON is a naked noun phrase, not a clause with a verb. Ask: which box word can take a point in time straight after it, and partners HAS NOT BRIGHTENED?",
                "explanation": "SINCE + a point in time = from that moment until now, and it partners a present perfect: SINCE noon, the sky HAS NOT brightened."
              },
              {
                "num": 8,
                "answer": "unless",
                "hint": "The match is CANCELLED, and the one thing that can save it is the RAIN stopping within THIRTY MINUTES. Ask: which box word means 'if not'? 'Because' would say the rain caused the cancellation, which is backwards.",
                "explanation": "UNLESS = if not. The match will be cancelled UNLESS the rain stops = it will be cancelled IF the rain does NOT stop. UNLESS = negative condition."
              }
