            "hint": "'ALTHOUGH' already carries the contrast, so the two halves must not fight twice. Ask: if 'although' opens the sentence, may you still drop 'but' into the middle? Decide which half is the surprise before you write.",
            "explanation": "ALTHOUGH introduces a contrast clause. ALTHOUGH the results were unexpected, the students STILL wrote a clear conclusion. NEVER use 'but' after 'although' — 'although' already shows the contrast.",
